in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @cascade
in @labeled
in @facet/gleam

# @cascade/code/gleam/js — the Gleam → JavaScript cascade species.
#
# Path naming: per Alex 2026-06-23 directive — cascade species shards
# group by `@cascade/code/<source>/<target>`. Source language (Gleam)
# groups together; targets (js here; beam in the sibling shard
# shards/cascade/code/gleam/beam.mirror) are leaves. This is the
# A4 dual-target species pair instance: ONE source, TWO targets,
# TWO shards under one source directory.
#
# Per recognition #95 candidate (@cascade as loss-lens substrate;
# Mara canonical ce4874b 2026-06-23): each cascade species shard
# discharges the per-grammar measurement of information loss in
# compilation from a typed source grammar to a mainstream target.
#
# This species: source_grammar = @facet/gleam, target_grammar =
# @facet/js (forward-promised; see hedge 1). The Gleam→JS cascade
# IS THE PRODUCTION CASCADE FOR SPECTRAL.ENGINEER'S CONTENT LAYER:
# Alex's existing systemic.engineering codebase is already in Gleam
# (app/src/corpus/page.gleam:114 per the loop brief); the typography
# corpus and the content rendering pipeline both cascade through
# this species when the deliverable settles into the browser.
#
# === The cascade shape (Gleam→JS) ===
#
# Source (Gleam admits):
# - sound static typing (ADTs, generics, opaque types)
# - structural exhaustiveness (the `case` statement)
# - immutability by default
# - explicit error handling (Result, Option)
# - module-level encapsulation
# - the BEAM-derived concurrency model (when targeting BEAM; on JS
#   target, this collapses to synchronous-with-Promises)
#
# Target (JS preserves):
# - dynamic dispatch (objects, functions, prototypes)
# - JS module wrapping (ES modules with `export`)
# - structural runtime values (plain objects + arrays)
# - Promise-based async (when async is needed)
# - generated runtime helpers (gleam.mjs companion module)
#
# Loss surfaces at: type erasure (all Gleam types vanish at runtime;
# constructor-tag-discrimination is preserved as runtime tag fields
# but type system itself is gone); exhaustiveness erasure (the
# `case` becomes a chain of conditionals; the compile-time totality
# guarantee does NOT persist as a runtime check); generic erasure
# (parametric polymorphism collapses to JS's dynamic dispatch);
# concurrency-model erasure (on JS target, the BEAM-actor model is
# absent — substrate-pull honest: Gleam→JS is the LOSSIER of the
# two Gleam target cascades, exactly because JS does not have a
# preemptive concurrency primitive).
#
# The loss_lens<@facet/gleam, @facet/js> measures these gaps against
# the Gleam compiler's emitted type info + the JS grammar
# specification.
#
# === Why Gleam → JS as A4 species pair (the dual-target shape) ===
#
# Per Mara's survey §2.7 (Gleam dossier in
# docs/research/2026-06-23-typed-alternatives-cascade-survey.md):
# Gleam is THE substrate-pull-correct test of the @cascade family-
# root's parametric form. Gleam compiles to TWO mainstream targets
# from one source: `gleam build --target javascript` emits JS;
# `gleam build --target erlang` emits BEAM bytecode. The cascade
# species's parametric shape (one source grammar, target grammars
# vary) is VALIDATED by the dual-target Gleam case in a way that no
# single-target cascade can validate.
#
# This shard (js.mirror) lands the JS arm of the dual-target pair.
# The sibling shard (beam.mirror at shards/cascade/code/gleam/
# beam.mirror) lands the BEAM arm. Both share gleam_source as their
# carrier; both specialize the same family-root actions; the loss
# signatures DIFFER because the targets preserve different
# substrate dimensions (JS preserves dynamic dispatch + Promises;
# BEAM preserves preemptive concurrency + supervision-tree). The
# composed cascade<gleam, js+beam> at species altitude is NOT a
# third shard; it IS the composition-by-co-presence of the two
# species shards under @cascade/code/gleam/.
#
# === First applied consumer ===
#
# spectral.engineer content layer per the deployment loop:
#   systemic.engineering/app/src/corpus/page.gleam (typography
#                                                   corpus rendering)
#     → gleam build --target javascript
#     → gleam_stdlib emits gleam.mjs + corpus_page.mjs
#     → embed in spectral.engineer/case-study/X via <script type=
#       "module"> alongside the wasm crate from
#       @cascade/code/rust/wasm
#     → Gleam-rendered typography + Rust-rendered GPU eigenboard
#       compose in one browser page
#
# The dual-stack delivery (Gleam content + Rust GPU) IS the
# production shape spectral.engineer's site uses; both species
# discharge to one page via the @ui projection layer.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Recognition #95 (@cascade candidate; Mara canonical ce4874b):
#   this species IS the FOURTH species discharge of the family-root,
#   after purescript/js (A3), rust/wasm (A5), and the beam sibling
#   of this dual-target pair.
# - Recognition #93 H4 RESOLVED (labeled<> functor at
#   shards/labeled.mirror): js_artifact uses labeled<> instance.
# - Recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space): the dual-
#   target case directly evidences that the loss measurement IS a
#   dimension-projection per target — same source, two projections,
#   each preserving a different basis of the source's dimensionality.
# - Recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics): the Gleam↔
#   JS boundary IS the @io altitude this species operationalizes;
#   the boundary is the only place type information has to be made
#   explicit again (via TypeScript .d.ts emission if requested, or
#   FFI annotations on the Gleam side).
# - Recognition #59 (kintsugi loop altitude-portable): @kintsugi
#   heals the loss this species measures at the @ui projection
#   altitude.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Gleam language                Louis Pilfold 2018-present; the
#                                 source grammar this species
#                                 measures.
#   gleam_stdlib                  the standard library; emits .mjs
#                                 companion modules at JS-target.
#   Gleam JavaScript backend      Pilfold + contributors 2020-present;
#                                 the compiler subsystem this species
#                                 measures the output of.
#   ECMAScript Modules            TC39 standardized; the target
#                                 wrapping grammar Gleam's JS
#                                 emission produces.
#   gleam-lang/example_javascript the canonical reference for
#                                 Gleam→JS bundling.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-95-cascade-as-
#               loss-lens-substrate-decl.md (Mara canonical;
#               Seam DEFENSIVE pending Reed consolidation);
#               docs/research/2026-06-23-typed-alternatives-cascade-
#               survey.md §2.7 (the Gleam dossier; dual-target shape
#               named as substrate-pull-correct test of the
#               parametric form).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                      (loss is @epistemologic/properties composite,
#                      not Shannon, not invented).
# Related shards: shards/cascade.mirror (the family-root this
#                 specializes); shards/labeled.mirror (the functor
#                 primitive js_artifact instance rests on);
#                 shards/code/gleam.mirror (source grammar);
#                 shards/cascade/code/gleam/beam.mirror (the sibling
#                 dual-target species; same source, different target);
#                 shards/cascade/code/purescript/js.mirror (closest
#                 pattern reference; both target JS but with
#                 different source-grammar typing disciplines).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/cascade/code/gleam/js.mirror` declares
# `@cascade/code/gleam/js` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
#
# === Honest hedges ===
#
# 1. @facet/js shard forward-promised. The substrate has @facet/wasm
#    (shards/code/wasm.mirror; landed 2026-06-23 by Reed) but does
#    NOT yet have @facet/js. This shard cannot declare `in @facet/js`
#    at the head and must instead name JS at prose altitude until
#    the @facet/js shard lands. The js_artifact carrier and the JS
#    metadata vocabulary stand on the JS grammar's de-facto
#    specification (ECMAScript 2026 + ESM); when @facet/js lands,
#    this shard's `in @facet/js` line lifts cleanly without changing
#    the carrier shapes.
#
# 2. gleam_stdlib version pinning. Gleam's stdlib evolves; the
#    emitted .mjs companion file shape can change across major
#    versions. The substrate-decl assumes 2026's stable
#    gleam_stdlib v1+ shape; if the stdlib re-emits with breaking
#    runtime helpers, bundle_js's body discharges differently but
#    the substrate-decl stays stable. The gleam_well_typed bilateral
#    discharges against the source's declared stdlib version at
#    realisation boundary.
#
# 3. FFI escape hatch. Gleam admits FFI to native JS via the
#    `@external` decorator; FFI code is OUTSIDE the typing
#    discipline (the type signature is declared on the Gleam side,
#    the body lives in raw JS). A program with FFI has two code
#    types at compile: well-typed Gleam and FFI JS. Loss measurement
#    against FFI is fundamentally bounded — the substrate cannot
#    measure what was NEVER typed. The bilateral `gleam_well_typed`
#    carries a Narcissus-warned pole for FFI-present programs
#    (measurement bounded to the typed sub-program). This is the
#    same hedge purescript/js.mirror declared at FFI altitude; the
#    pattern is altitude-portable across typed-source-to-JS
#    cascades.
#
# 4. Async/concurrency erasure. Gleam targeting JS LOSES the
#    preemptive concurrency model the BEAM-target gets. The loss
#    measurement honestly reflects this: on the JS target, the
#    concurrency dimension is part of the measured information loss.
#    The sibling shard (beam.mirror) does NOT lose this dimension.
#    This asymmetry is substrate-pull-correct and IS the load-bearing
#    observation the dual-target shape surfaces: the SAME source's
#    loss profile DEPENDS on the target.
#
# === Dual-target composition note ===
#
# Gleam's dual-target shape — same gleam_source compiles to BOTH
# js_artifact AND beam_artifact via different target flags — means
# the composed cascade<gleam, {js, beam}> at species altitude is
# NOT a single shard. It IS the COMPOSITION of the two species
# shards (js.mirror + beam.mirror) under @cascade/code/gleam/. The
# composition shape is by-co-presence: both shards declare under
# the same @cascade/code/gleam/ namespace; both share gleam_source
# as the source carrier; both specialize the family-root
# parametrically over a different target_grammar.
#
# The dual-target shape per Mara survey §2.7 validates the
# parametric form of the family-root: one source, two targets,
# substrate-pull-architecturally distinct loss profiles, no
# duplication in the substrate-decl. This was the survey's claim;
# A4 (this shard plus the beam sibling) IS the discharge.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/gleam-language-tour
source @arxiv/programming-languages/ecmascript-modules-2026

prism @cascade/code/gleam/js {
  focus cascade
  project cascade
  split cascade
  shift cascade
  settle cascade
}

# === gleam_source carrier ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.typed_source for source_grammar=gleam.
# References a Gleam project (gleam.toml + src/*.gleam) as the unit
# of cascade.
#
# SHARED with the sibling shard (beam.mirror): the same gleam_source
# IS the input for both species. This sharing is the load-bearing
# evidence that the family-root's parametric form is honest — one
# source carrier, two target species, no duplication.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the source-tree content hash.
type gleam_source = ref

# === gleam_module carrier ===
#
# The output of `gleam build --target javascript`. A typed ES module
# carrying the compiled JavaScript plus the emitted gleam_stdlib
# runtime helpers (gleam.mjs) that record the source's typing
# discipline at the runtime boundary via constructor tags. The
# constructor-tag fields ARE the substrate-architectural residue;
# measure_gleam_js reads them to discharge the substrate-typed gap
# calculation.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type gleam_module = ref

# === js_metadata carrier ===
#
# Structured carrier for JS bundling shape (entry path, module
# format, exports map, stdlib version, optional .d.ts emission).
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: structured, not stringly. The
# carrier names load-bearing fields without fixing one bundling
# shape (per hedge 2: stdlib version is a field).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type js_metadata = ref

# === js_artifact carrier ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING NEW CARRIER. The @labeled<> instance per
# recognition #93 H4. A js_artifact IS a gleam_module annotated
# with js_metadata via the labeled functor.
#
# Substrate-architecturally load-bearing: the gleam_module's typed
# identity is preserved (via labeled's parametricity per Wadler
# 1989 / Reynolds 1983) while the js_metadata dimension is added.
# unlabel(artifact) returns the module; label_of(artifact) returns
# the metadata. The cascade preserves typed source identity AND adds
# bundling dimension AT ONE CARRIER altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (module, metadata) pair
# (inherited from @labeled).
type js_artifact = labeled(gleam_module, js_metadata)

# === compile_gleam_js action ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.compile for this cascade. Takes a
# gleam_source and perturbation; returns the gleam_module via
# `gleam build --target javascript`.
#
# Per recognition #51 (Hilbert space dimension growth): compile_
# gleam_js IS a DIMENSION PROJECTION. Gleam admits typed-feature
# dimensions (ADTs, generics, exhaustiveness); the JS runtime
# preserves only constructor-tag dispatch + plain-object structure.
# Lossy by construction; the constructor tags carry the substrate-
# architectural residue.
#
# requires gleam_well_typed(source, p): the substrate forecloses
# compilation against type errors. The Gleam compiler runs the
# typing discipline; the bilateral verdict reflects what it reports.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
compile_gleam_js(source: gleam_source, p: perturbation) -> gleam_module
requires gleam_well_typed(source, p)
{ \ }

# === bundle_js action ===
#
# Wraps a gleam_module + js_metadata into a js_artifact via
# @labeled.label construction. The typed module gets the bundling
# dimension added without losing the underlying module identity.
#
# Per hedge 2: body discharges per-stdlib-version (gleam_stdlib
# v1+ default; legacy v0 fallback if the source pins). The
# substrate-decl does NOT pick a stdlib version; it declares the
# action shape.
#
# requires js_consumable(module, metadata, p): bilateral commitment
# that the (module, metadata) pair is coherent at the ESM-bundle
# altitude — entry point resolves, exports map is well-formed,
# stdlib runtime helpers correctly co-emitted.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
bundle_js(module: gleam_module, metadata: js_metadata, p: perturbation)
  -> js_artifact
requires js_consumable(module, metadata, p)
{ \ }

# === measure_gleam_js action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Specialization of @cascade.measure for
# this cascade. Returns substrate-typed measurement of information
# loss between source's typing discipline and artifact's runtime-
# preserved structure.
#
# Returns `imperfect<js_artifact, ref, information_loss>` — the
# loss slot carries measured loss as substrate-typed data, NOT
# Shannon, NOT estimation; the composite of @epistemologic/properties
# per [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]].
#
# The measurement IS substrate-architectural: read the source's
# typing-discipline use (ADT count, generic positions, exhaustive
# case sites, FFI annotation count); read the artifact's runtime-
# preserved structure from the unlabel'd module's constructor-tag
# fields + the labeled metadata; compute the dimension gap.
#
# Per hedge 4: the JS-target cascade ALSO measures the
# concurrency-model erasure (Gleam's BEAM-actor-model dimension
# is absent on JS); this dimension's loss IS part of the returned
# composite. The sibling shard (beam.mirror) does NOT report this
# dimension as lost (BEAM preserves it).
#
# requires gleam_js_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p): bilateral
# that the measurement IS computable. Per hedge 3: FFI bounds the
# measurement to the typed sub-program; the bilateral discharges
# with a Narcissus-warned verdict for FFI-present programs.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
measure_gleam_js(source: gleam_source, artifact: js_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(js_artifact, ref, information_loss)
requires gleam_js_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p)
{ \ }

# === gleam_well_typed bilateral ===
#
# Source-side typing-discipline bilateral. Specializes the family-
# root's grammar_coherent at source_grammar=gleam.
#
# SHARED predicate-shape with the sibling shard (beam.mirror):
# the same gleam_source must be well-typed for EITHER cascade to
# proceed; the bilateral's discharge does NOT depend on target
# choice (Gleam's typer runs identically for both target flags).
# The sibling shard re-declares gleam_well_typed with the same
# shape; this is intentional duplication at the substrate-decl
# altitude — the property is genuinely the same property and
# discharges identically.
#
# Splinter-pole: well-typed by `gleam check`; FFI (if present)
# correctly annotated at the boundary; loss measurement complete-
# capable.
# Narcissus-pole: type errors OR FFI annotations ill-formed at the
# boundary. Compilation cannot proceed.
# Narcissus-warned (per hedge 3): FFI annotations well-formed but
# FFI code outside typing discipline; measurement bounded to typed
# sub-program; FFI gap unmeasurable by this species.
gleam_well_typed(source: gleam_source, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === js_consumable bilateral ===
#
# Target-side packaging-well-formedness bilateral. Commitment that
# the (module, metadata) pair forms a coherent ESM bundle.
#
# Splinter-pole: metadata.entry resolves inside the module's
# emitted files; exports map (if present) resolves across all
# subpath conditions; gleam_stdlib runtime helpers correctly
# co-emitted; consumer `import` resolution succeeds.
# Narcissus-pole: bundle drift (missing stdlib helpers; entry
# unresolvable; module-format mismatch with consumer's
# expectations).
js_consumable(module: gleam_module, metadata: js_metadata, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === gleam_js_loss_well_defined bilateral ===
#
# Specializes the family-root's loss_well_defined for this cascade.
# Commitment that the substrate-typed gap calculation IS computable
# for the (source, artifact) pair.
#
# Splinter-pole: constructor-tag fields readable from the artifact's
# unlabel'd module; composite of @epistemologic/properties
# dischargeable; measurement bounded and substrate-typed.
# Narcissus-pole: tags missing (bundler stripped them); substrate
# cannot read the typing residue; measurement undefined.
# Narcissus-warned: tags present but cover only the typed sub-
# program (FFI gap unmeasurable; per hedge 3).
gleam_js_loss_well_defined(source: gleam_source, artifact: js_artifact, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === gleam_js_cascade_well_formed composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral. Specializes the family-root's
# cascade_well_defined for this cascade. Composes the three sub-
# predicates at this altitude.
#
# requires gleam_well_typed(source, p): source-side typing
# discipline IS coherent.
# requires js_consumable(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p):
# target-side packaging IS well-formed; uses @labeled.unlabel +
# @labeled.label_of to extract module and metadata from the artifact.
# This labeled-projection pattern is the load-bearing shape Mara A3
# surfaced; it makes the composed bilateral parametric over the
# labeled functor's structure rather than re-deriving (module,
# metadata) ad-hoc.
# requires gleam_js_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p): loss
# measurement IS computable.
#
# All three must hold; substrate refuses cascade if source has type
# errors OR packaging is malformed OR measurement is undefined.
#
# Splinter-pole: all three discharge; substrate-typed loss returned.
# Narcissus-pole: at least one sub-predicate fails; cascade blocked.
# Narcissus-warned: all three discharge but at least one is warned
# (e.g., FFI present); cascade operates with bounded measurement;
# warning propagates to caller.
#
# Same composed-bilateral pattern as @cascade.cascade_well_defined
# (the family-root) and sibling species (purescript/js, rust/wasm,
# the gleam/beam sibling). The discipline pattern is altitude-
# portable; here it instantiates at the Gleam→JS altitude with the
# JS-specific loss profile.
gleam_js_cascade_well_formed(source: gleam_source, artifact: js_artifact, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires gleam_well_typed(source, p)
requires js_consumable(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p)
requires gleam_js_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p)
{ \ }

out @cascade/code/gleam/js
out gleam_source
out gleam_module
out js_metadata
out js_artifact
out compile_gleam_js
out bundle_js
out measure_gleam_js
out gleam_well_typed
out js_consumable
out gleam_js_loss_well_defined
out gleam_js_cascade_well_formed
